# `FROM` in capitals after `|` (DS0152), which used to be DS0105 with no help.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | FROM x
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..16
  PIPELINE@0..15
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    ERROR@9..15
      IDENT@9..13 "FROM"
      WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
      IDENT@14..15 "x"
  WHITESPACE@15..16 "\n"

error[DS0152]: `from` is not an operator
  --> query:1:10
  |
1 | from t | FROM x
  |        - ^^^^ `from` starts a query; after `|` comes an operator
  |        |
  |        this `|` has no operator after it
  |
  = help: to start a new query, end the previous one with `;` instead of `|`
  = help: to combine two tables, use `union` or `join`: `| union t`
